# ---- Secrets (never commit) ----
fmpAPIkey.txt

# ---- Large data artifacts (sync out-of-band, never in git; GitHub rejects >100MB) ----
*.pickle
*.pkl
baseline_tools/price_data/

# ---- Generated output / results ----
output/
results/
# NOTE: the presentations/ HTML (the CEO's picks) is DELIBERATELY TRACKED per CEO
# decision 2026-07-17 — it travels with the pipeline. Do NOT re-add an ignore for it.
# Root-level result artifacts emitted by a pipeline run (NEVER commit — they are
# regenerated every run and can leak the ranked output). Dated variants match too.
AggScoreTop*.csv
PresentationTop*.xlsx
ForensicFlagsTop*.csv
# Generated tune/backtest result dumps (regenerated every run; never commit).
*.out
# Real price data (moves via Google Drive only, never git). price_data/ already
# covered above; these also guard root-level copies.
real_prices.csv
real_prices_2025.csv

# Delisted-entity ingestion DATA artifacts (multi-GB, move via Google Drive only,
# never git): registry parquet, dead fundamentals pickle, bulk prices, death
# signature, resume anchor. The compact run_logs/ MANIFEST + JSONL travel via
# GitHub and are DELIBERATELY NOT ignored (how the house inspects a run).
delisted_out/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# ---- Logs ----
logs/
*.log

# ---- IDE ----
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- OS / app cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.~lock.*#
RawMetricsTop100*.csv
CohortMetricStats*.csv
SideList_*.csv
MarketCapBand_*.csv

# ---- Run-emitted AUDIT CSVs (2026-07-25) ----
# Dated, regenerated every run, and they name universe members -- same class as the
# result artifacts above, so the same rule: never commit. They were untracked but NOT
# ignored, so a `git add -A` would have swept them in (review R-N5).
ExcludedShareClasses_*.csv
CurrencyFloorFlips_*.csv
ReportingFrequencyConflicts_*.csv
# Universe-provenance sidecar (2026-08-03): dated, regenerated every run, and for a
# curated universe it lists the member symbols -- same class as the above.
RunProvenance-*.json

# ---- MISPLACED evidence CSVs written by a pytest run (2026-08-22) ----
# `carveOut` writes its dedup/currency evidence to `_tu.EVIDENCE_DIR`, which resolves
# relative to the CWD.  A pytest invocation whose CWD is `baseline_tools/` therefore drops
# `DedupSurvivorReport_<date>.csv` THERE instead of at the repo root, untracked and NOT
# ignored -- a reviewer had to delete one by hand after its own suite run.
#
# SCOPED TO baseline_tools/ ON PURPOSE.  The ROOT-level `DedupSurvivorReport_*.csv` files
# are deliberately TRACKED (five of them, cited as provenance by exclusions.py), so a
# blanket pattern would silently stop the next legitimate evidence file being committed.
# Only the wrong-directory copy is ignored.  The real fix is carveOut's CWD-dependent
# EVIDENCE_DIR, which is not this change set's surface.
baseline_tools/DedupSurvivorReport_*.csv

# ---- Offline measurement artifacts (2026-07-27) ----
# Same class again: regenerated by baseline_tools/decile_test.py + panel_upgrade.py, they
# name universe members, and the panel cache is ~120 MB (over GitHub's hard limit). The
# *.pickle rule above already covers the cache; these make the intent explicit and cover
# the CSV siblings.
baseline_tools/decile_*.csv
baseline_tools/attribution_*.csv
baseline_tools/conditional_*.csv
baseline_tools/anchor_check_*.csv
baseline_tools/confound_*.csv
baseline_tools/industry_attribution.csv
baseline_tools/refit_runlog_*.json
baseline_tools/refit_grid_*.csv
baseline_tools/CORRECTED_*.csv
# Per-exchange completeness tables (2026-08-03): 12 generated CSVs from
# baseline_tools/per_exchange_completeness.py. Same class as the CORRECTED_/decile_ tables
# above -- regenerated on demand and they name universe members. The PRODUCER (.py) is a
# deliberate deliverable and stays tracked; only its output is ignored.
baseline_tools/pxc_*.csv
baseline_tools/resdic_*.pickle
baseline_tools/cache_panel_*
baseline_tools/cache_stage1_*
baseline_tools/psm_*.pickle

# generated analysis / diagnostic outputs (never source)
loo_*.csv
baseline_tools/loo_*.csv
MissingDataFillReport_*.csv
ReportingFrequencyConflicts_*.csv

# quarantined generated artifacts (never source)
_quarantine/
ManualEliminationTickersList_fmp_*.csv
# its dated, schema-carrying replacement (2026-08-14).  NOTE the pattern deliberately does
# NOT cover the un-dated `ExclusionList_fmp.csv`: that one is the file the CEO CURATES and
# arms by hand, so if it ever exists it should be tracked, not ignored.
ExclusionList_*_*.csv
InputSanityRefusals_*.csv
delisted_tickers_*.csv

# Generated measurement-report text artifacts (baseline_tools/nan_policy_report.py and friends).
# Same class as the *.csv / *.xlsx result artifacts above: reproducible from the script, ~300 KB
# each, and full of progress-bar noise. The SCRIPT is tracked; its output is not.
baseline_tools/nan_policy_report_*.txt
baseline_tools/cache_nanpolicy_*.pickle

# pick_log.csv is a PER-MACHINE append-only forensic record, not source.
# It was tracked until 2026-08-22, which collided with the auto-quarantine added in ce52e73:
# a local run renames it into the gitignored _quarantine/, so git saw a tracked file vanish
# and a restore would trigger a second quarantine with a -2 suffix. Untracked deliberately.
pick_log.csv

# The run machine put its old price grids here during the 2026-08-28 refetch and they were
# swept into a commit. They are `real_prices*` under another name -- the standing rule is that
# those never enter git. Untracked 2026-08-31; the files themselves are untouched on disk.
temp/
